---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Async Forest"
  description="Henry Franks: fifteen years as a startup founder, CTO, and chief architect; a Warwick PhD on trust in open systems of autonomous agents; guest lecturer on responsible AI at King's College London and Notre Dame."
>
  <section class="about container container--narrow">
    <div class="about__head">
      <div>
        <h1>Henry Franks</h1>
        <p class="about__thesis-marker mono">[THESIS SLOT — being written]</p>
        <p class="about__lede">
          I've spent my career building and architecting production software
          and AI systems — as a founder, CTO, and chief architect — and
          teaching the responsible-AI side of the field at King's College
          London and Notre Dame. My doctoral research was on trust and
          cooperation in open systems of autonomous agents.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about__photo" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="mono">[PHOTO SLOT — headshot]</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about__body">
      <h2>Career</h2>
      <p>
        I'm based in London. Over fifteen-plus years I've been a startup
        founder and CTO, a principal engineer, a data scientist, and a chief
        architect, across energy, insurance and data, and climate-policy AI.
        I'm currently chief architect at a climate-policy AI non-profit. The
        work has stayed hands-on throughout: full-stack systems, cloud
        infrastructure on AWS, data and ML, and GenAI in production.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most people who talk about responsible AI haven't shipped production
        systems; most people shipping GenAI don't dwell on the responsibility
        part. My work has always sat where the two meet.
      </p>

      <h2>Research</h2>
      <p>
        My PhD, from the University of Warwick, asked how trust, reputation,
        and cooperation emerge in open systems of autonomous agents. The
        publications have around 140 citations, mainly at AAMAS and in
        Springer journals — <a href="[SCHOLAR LINK SLOT]">Google Scholar</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Teaching</h2>
      <p>
        I guest lecture annually on responsible AI at King's College London
        and the University of Notre Dame. Some of the frameworks I teach and
        use in engagements are written up under
        <a href="/writing/#models">models</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The practice</h2>
      <p>
        Async Forest Ltd is the company through which I consult — a UK limited
        company with professional indemnity insurance. The judgement is mine;
        the engagement is with the company.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="about__close">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Tell me about the decision you're facing</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--section-y) var(--space-8);
  }
  .about__head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 200px;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .about__thesis-marker {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .about__lede {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .about__photo {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--surface-warm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }

  .about__body h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .about__close {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about__head {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
    .about__photo { max-width: 200px; }
  }
</style>
